index 0000000..bdcd4c4
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/research/warning-policy-audit.md
@@ -0,0 +1,102 @@
+# Compiler warning audit
+
+## Baseline and scope
+
+Baseline: `4197a91f662bf81f19de1409efd8a331b6dca16e`.
+The root Makefile orchestrates submakes; adding unused root CFLAGS would
+not establish a compiler policy. `share/mk/sys.mk` selected optimization
+flags but no common fatal-warning policy. Several leaves replaced CFLAGS.
+The RP2040 kernel selected `-Wall -Werror`, without `-Wextra`. The STM32
+and PIC32 kernel warning sets were less strict and remain a separate
+migration; this change does not claim those kernels are extra-warning clean.
+
+Standalone tools use `tools/Makefile.inc`, not the shared target compiler.
+Zoneinfo and the Linux smux build replace CC with HOST_CC. The awk and game
+build generators invoke HOST_CC directly. These are separate enforcement
+paths, and all receive the common fatal-warning flag in the repair.
+Existing stricter per-tool flags, C dialects, ABI flags and optimization
+choices remain in place.
+
+## Measured warning inventory
+
+An isolated Ubuntu 24.04 build with ARM GCC 13.2.1 enabled the extra
+warning groups in both RP2040 kernels and the shared ARM userland command.
+Warnings were nonfatal only in that disposable diagnostic checkout. The
+build completed and its final warning assertion intentionally failed.
+GitHub Actions run: `35296347256`, investigation commit
+`a4503baa2e11ac7cb22dfc75bde711e41b265b8b`.
+
+The two kernel configurations emitted 231 warning instances:
+
+| Group | Instances |
+| --- | ---: |
+| unused parameter | 108 |
+| signed/unsigned comparison | 100 |
+| implicit fallthrough | 11 |
+| setjmp clobber analysis | 8 |
+| empty body | 2 |
+| enum type limits | 2 |
+
+The full expanded-warning build emitted 8,559 compiler-warning instances,
+including repeated headers and both kernel configurations. These counts
+are not counts of distinct defects. Enabling every warning group throughout
+the inherited userland in one patch would conflate a much larger source
+migration with this enforcement repair. The userland change instead makes
+its currently selected warnings fatal, with no new group-wide suppression.
+
+## Source decisions
+
+Device and legacy interface parameters remain in their signatures; explicit
+void uses mark arguments that a configuration does not consume. Intentional
+switch fallthroughs are annotated. A dead default-path log in dupfdopen now
+has an explicit return, rather than an unrecognized fallthrough comment.
+
+Bounded indices, syscall sizes, and signed sentinels use explicit matching
+types. `sysctl_file` and `sysctl_doproc` keep buffer lengths in size_t
+rather than narrowing user-supplied lengths to int. The executable-header
+checks compare against a bounded signed sizeof value, also rejecting a
+negative supplied header length rather than promoting it to unsigned.
+
+The narrow signed p_uid field is not changed: its layout belongs to the
+kernel ABI. Explicit uid_t conversions preserve the previous unsigned
+comparison semantics. Full-range UID representation and negative resource
+limit policy are not repaired or certified by this warning cleanup.
+
+The next-fit allocator checks unsigned addition wrap directly. Its host
+gate now distinguishes a genuinely wrapping wide descriptor from a compact
+descriptor whose end crosses 16 bits but still fits size_t.
+
+Device and syscall dispatch pointers are initialized once before setjmp.
+The rewritten vn_open mode stays in volatile storage for the existing
+returns-twice checkpoint. The checkpoint is not extracted into a helper:
+cleanup can still sleep, so u_qsave must not reference a returned frame.
+This is not a claim that GCC's prior clobber warnings prove an observed
+board failure.
+
+## Validation and remaining boundaries
+
+The repair adds clean-control/deliberate-warning gates to the root host and
+cross tiers. Original-tree host and shared-target commands accept the bad
+probe; the repaired commands reject it. Both kernel builds reject separate
+Wall-only and Wextra-only probes. Host probes also pass with Clang.
+`sys/arch/rp2040/doc/TESTING.md` defines the policy and gate contract.
+
+Local ARM GCC 13.2.1 builds of both kernels are warning-free. The measured
+ELF section sizes are:
+
+| Configuration | Baseline text | Repaired text | Data (unchanged) | BSS (unchanged) |
+| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |
+| PICO | 103058 | 103026 | 248 | 39544 |
+| PICO_UART | 90928 | 90888 | 192 | 14528 |
+
+These are compilation/link measurements, not board or emulator execution.
+The kernel-source host gates, config generator test, swapram evacuation
+and a.out header tests were run separately. The local full-world build
+requires nroff beyond the recovered toolchain; the standard firmware CI
+is the full-build authority, not a partial local log. No UF2 conversion,
+Renode boot, or physical board result is inferred from linking an ELF.
+
+Remaining work: migrate userland warning groups in bounded source families;
+validate the inherited STM32/PIC32 build matrices; review existing local
+warning suppressions; track compiler flags as userland object dependencies;
+and add build-generator probes where direct HOST_CC recipes are introduced.
